		{
			"id": "T-2ky2NT6t5E0ShRp",
			"name": "Pariah Gene (Blank)",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A blank is born, not made: a rare genetic absence that leaves a person's soul all but invisible in the warp, and makes the warp itself recoil from them. Psykers, daemons, and even animals find blanks instinctively unsettling to be near — a \"hole\" where a presence should be. Depicted consistently across Black Library (the Culexus Temple's \"Untouchables,\" Cain-series and Eisenhorn-cycle blanks) and Dark Heresy/Only War's Untouchable career.\n\nDesign: Deliberately carries no Warp Sorcery or Perils of the Warp modifier, and needs no Warp Empowerment: a Pariah's field is the *absence* of the warp, not a channelled act, so none of the framework's activation risk or spell-cost cap applies. See each child trait for its own derivation. Net for the package: +12 (Null Aura) +10 (Immunity) -3 (Unnerving Void) -10 (Social Stigma) = +9.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Psyker",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tzi2GqL6XH8_-nz9a",
					"name": "Null Aura",
					"local_notes": "Lore: The blank's presence itself smothers nearby psychic workings — the basis for why the Inquisition uses blanks to hunt witches and why daemons fear and hate them.\n\nDesign: Built on Affliction (Basic B35): base 10, the delivered \"Warp- Choked\" disadvantage is valued at -30 points for the enhancement math (+30%), stacked with Area Effect (+50%, B102, 2-yard radius), Always On (-40%, B113, it can't be switched off or aimed), and Emanation (-20%, B111, no ranged attack roll, just proximity).",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "mIUNwXGaPAziCh01l",
							"name": "Disadvantage Delivered (Warp-Choked",
							"local_notes": "Any Warp-tagged ability used in the area must be rolled again as if failed; already-running continuous Warp effects go inert while inside it.",
							"cost_adj": "+30%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mWrAqiyQsVevR4Icz",
							"name": "Area Effect, 2 yards",
							"cost_adj": "+50%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mLASLvUCNJcnXop1s",
							"name": "Always On",
							"cost_adj": "-40%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mhEYNcbpwsYvfD0FC",
							"name": "Emanation",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						}
					],
					"base_points": 10
				},
				{
					"id": "tUfyETw9jEJKkZD-V",
					"name": "Immunity to Warp-Based Effects",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Warp-based Affliction, Mind Control, Mind Probe, and Fear simply do not work on a Pariah.\n\nDesign: Resistant (B81), Occasional hazard 10, Immunity x1 = 10. Warp-based attacks are treated as an \"occasional\" specific hazard for a Pariah, since it is their entire defining trait. Same \"base x1\" convention as the Grey Knights' Incorruptible.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"base_points": 10
				},
				{
					"id": "tWim4sSYekhNUDvZ5",
					"name": "Unnatural Features (Unnerving Void)",
					"local_notes": "Lore: People and animals find a Pariah's presence quietly, deeply wrong.\n\nDesign: Basic's Unnatural Features (per-level reaction penalty), 3 levels of -1 each.",
					"tags": [
						"Disadvantage",
						"Social",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"points_per_level": -1,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 3
				},
				{
					"id": "tuQMbcwUICSkJq-ED",
					"name": "Social Stigma (Feared Blank)",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Feared and, in many sectors, watched or conscripted by the Inquisition and the Officio Assassinorum.\n\nDesign: Basic's Social Stigma (Minority Group), -10 (B155).",
					"tags": [
						"Disadvantage",
						"Social",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"base_points": -10
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "TgtzKSsaAuyhxlTtT",
			"name": "Pariah Gene (Untouchable)",
			"local_notes": "Lore: An Untouchable is a blank whose gene runs stronger still — the raw material from which the Officio Assassinorum's Culexus Temple recruits. Their null field is wider, their touch is actively harmful to warp- spawned things, and ordinary people find them nearly impossible to be near for long. This trait models the degree only, not a full Culexus Assassin (animus speculum, etc. belong to that unit's own writeup).\n\nDesign: Same components as Pariah Gene, scaled up: wider Null Aura, a new Soul-Static Discharge that actively harms warp-touched creatures in contact, deeper social cost. Net: +22 (Null Aura) +5 (Soul-Static Discharge) +10 (Immunity) -5 (Unnerving Void) -15 (Social Stigma) = +17.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Psyker",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tFYERcJm87PyoRBo0",
					"name": "Null Aura (Wide)",
					"local_notes": "Lore: See Pariah Gene's Null Aura; the field simply reaches further.\n\nDesign: As Pariah Gene's Null Aura, but Area Effect scaled to the 8-yard tier (+150%, B102) instead of 2 yards.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "mRJ9JAWQWKz3QPLlk",
							"name": "Disadvantage Delivered (Warp-Choked",
							"cost_adj": "+30%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mdzgiyCNfvzEEnjUR",
							"name": "Area Effect, 8 yards",
							"cost_adj": "+150%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mVHaRXKF6xqYvdkrR",
							"name": "Always On",
							"cost_adj": "-40%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mw5mq6l3XNxdfWLPN",
							"name": "Emanation",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						}
					],
					"base_points": 10
				},
				{
					"id": "tC0qhiHHyO9Oumh-7",
					"name": "Soul-Static Discharge",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Warp-spawned creatures — daemons, Chaos Spawn, warp-touched beasts — burn where an Untouchable's field touches them.\n\nDesign: Innate Attack (Toxic, 4/die, B61) with Aura (+80%, B111, automatic contact damage), Always On (-40%), and Accessibility limiting it to warp-touched targets only (-20%).",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "mWAM_-nT_gzH2fle4",
							"name": "Aura",
							"cost_adj": "+80%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mscN1SozbwJApy1w6",
							"name": "Always On",
							"cost_adj": "-40%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mUXXBOEro-HZR_sK0",
							"name": "Accessibility (only vs. Warp-touched/daemonic creatures)",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						}
					],
					"points_per_level": 4,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 1
				},
				{
					"id": "tsozPwTFE-0zGkZtO",
					"name": "Immunity to Warp-Based Effects",
					"local_notes": "Lore: As Pariah Gene.\n\nDesign: As Pariah Gene's Immunity to Warp-Based Effects.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"base_points": 10
				},
				{
					"id": "tX5YjLtKK88pDUyvx",
					"name": "Unnatural Features (Unnerving Void, Deep)",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Few can stand to be near an Untouchable for long.\n\nDesign: As Pariah Gene, at 5 levels instead of 3.",
					"tags": [
						"Disadvantage",
						"Social",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"points_per_level": -1,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 5
				},
				{
					"id": "tq9V8UYASURyY8Dk3",
					"name": "Social Stigma (Monster)",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Treated by most Imperial citizens as barely human — when not simply recruited and vanished by the Officio Assassinorum.\n\nDesign: Basic's Social Stigma (Monster), -15 (B155).",
					"tags": [
						"Disadvantage",
						"Social",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"base_points": -15
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "TiHlJY8ogfOvJmJ2u",
			"name": "Navigator's Third Eye",
			"local_notes": "Lore: House Navigators carry a third eye, fused shut beneath the brow, that perceives the Astronomican's light and the safe currents of the warp well enough to steer a ship through it — and that kills or maddens anyone it meets uncovered. Navigators keep the eye bound at all times except when navigating from a shielded bridge. The clearest published detail on this comes from the Rogue Trader corebook's Navigator background rather than Black Library, which mostly gestures at the Navis Nobilite and the \"third eye\" in passing (e.g. Horus Heresy-era references); treat the RPG-tier material as the calibration source here per the framework's source-priority rule. Over centuries of psychic strain, aged Navigators are widely depicted as growing increasingly strange or deformed (a GM-invoked cosmetic/social disadvantage for very old Navigators — e.g. escalating Unnatural Features — rather than a fixed cost baked into this trait).\n\nDesign: Deliberately carries no Warp Sorcery or Perils of the Warp modifier, and needs no Warp Empowerment: the third eye is an always-on inherited mutation, not a deliberately channelled act — though a GM is free to call for a one-off Perils-style check during an extreme event like flying blind through a warp storm. Net for the package: 13 (Warp Sight: 5 x 2.5 = 12.5, rounded up) + 9 (Lethal Gaze: 10 x 0.9) = 22.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Psyker",
				"Imperium",
				"Navis Nobilite"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "t68YzDrZWKcg4xl8O",
					"name": "Warp Sight",
					"local_notes": "Lore: What lets a Navigator see the Astronomican's beacon and the warp's safer currents across a voyage, letting a ship cross the immaterium without being lost or devoured.\n\nDesign: Detect (Basic B47-48), base 5 for an uncommon, specific thing; Precise doubles that (expressed here as +100%, equivalent to Basic's x2 multiplier); Increased Range at the highest tabled step (+60%, the \"100x\" tier) reflects effectively unlimited range while the eye is open in transit; Accessibility (-10%) reflects that it only works, and is only tolerable, while uncovered.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium",
						"Navis Nobilite"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "mw-3ZVccJc_ucXv3a",
							"name": "Precise",
							"cost_adj": "+100%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mXIJ7Obt8DCk7YZ_9",
							"name": "Increased Range x100",
							"cost_adj": "+60%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mNqz8CYN_aReKeZ2o",
							"name": "Accessibility (only while the third eye is uncovered)",
							"cost_adj": "-10%"
						}
					],
					"base_points": 5,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "skill_bonus",
							"selection_type": "skills_with_name",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Navigation"
							},
							"amount": 4,
							"specialization": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Warp"
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "tKBA9G7efGskpgCnM",
					"name": "Lethal Gaze",
					"local_notes": "Lore: This is why the eye stays bound: anyone who meets it directly, with no warding, risks death or madness. It is a narrative hazard for the people around a Navigator far more than a usable weapon for the player.\n\nDesign: Affliction (Basic B35), base 10, delivering a -50 point \"Mind-Sundering\" disadvantage (+50%); Sense-Based (Vision) (-20%, B112, only affects those who can see the eye); Uncontrollable (-30%, B113, the Navigator cannot pick and choose who is struck); Accessibility limiting it to moments the eye is uncovered (-10%).",
					"tags": [
						"Disadvantage",
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium",
						"Navis Nobilite"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "mRCAbEkvELnGyOIGj",
							"name": "Disadvantage Delivered (Mind-Sundering",
							"local_notes": "An unshielded mortal who meets the open eye is killed, driven mad, or worse, GM's call; only other Navigators and comparably warp-touched beings routinely survive it.",
							"cost_adj": "+50%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mYhFszpYiqLV4JUkk",
							"name": "Sense-Based (Vision)",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mK_zGf19pKqB8I5XC",
							"name": "Uncontrollable",
							"cost_adj": "-30%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mIh5crKleullSdgwE",
							"name": "Accessibility (only when the third eye is uncovered)",
							"cost_adj": "-10%"
						}
					],
					"base_points": 10
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "TcrlRstYZlaIlQIxR",
			"name": "Biomancy",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The discipline of the flesh: hardening it, mending it, driving it faster than it should go, or unmaking an enemy's body from the inside. Calibrated against Dark Heresy's Biomancy power list (Smite, Iron Arm, Warp Speed, Haemorrhage all appear there under close-to-these names) and Black Library depictions of Biomancer-Librarians and Chaos \"physicians.\"\n\nDesign: Talent-linked group; see each child for build math. All children take Warp Sorcery (-20%) and Perils of the Warp (-10%) unless noted.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Psyker",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tfmwrnTbnQZqHGuX3",
					"name": "Smite",
					"local_notes": "Lore: A bolt of warp lightning that arcs from the psyker's hand and burns through armour, the way tabletop Smite's mortal wounds ignore it. On an average hit it drops an Astartes Battle-Brother (HP 34, torso DR 103) to the brink of death; a Guardsman is simply gone.\n\nDesign: Innate Attack (Burning, 5/die, B61) with Armor Divisor (10) (+200%, B103) plus Warp Sorcery/Perils, net +170%. Full modified cost: 5 x 2.7 = 13.5 points/level. Bought at 12 levels (12d(10) burn) for 162 points, the default a trained battlefield psyker buys; a lesser psyker may buy fewer levels. Math: 12d averages 42, and at (10) a Battle-Brother's DR 103 becomes about 10, so an average hit puts about 32 burn damage into HP 34 (two HP short of dead, and any roll above average finishes him). Needs Warp Empowerment level 16 (cap 170) at 12 levels, or level 1 (cap 20) for a single level.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "muEItWuUB87ABS-Vz",
							"name": "Armor Divisor (10)",
							"cost_adj": "+200%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mSwDr12GEICA1vNQ1",
							"name": "Warp Sorcery",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mBjrh3u1j4Ga_GD3H",
							"name": "Perils of the Warp",
							"cost_adj": "-10%"
						}
					],
					"points_per_level": 5,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 12
				},
				{
					"id": "tK8NsrSDvGepTHyLV",
					"name": "Endurance",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Wards off fatigue and pain in battle by forcing the body past its limits.\n\nDesign: Extra Fatigue Points (3/level, B ~power-ups table) with Warp Sorcery/Perils, net -30%. Full modified cost: ~2 points/level; needs Warp Empowerment level 1 (cap 20).",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "mb5WP-Vm6d0MiwQLF",
							"name": "Warp Sorcery",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mzbYjPSyTYaWxEUvp",
							"name": "Perils of the Warp",
							"cost_adj": "-10%"
						}
					],
					"points_per_level": 3,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 1
				},
				{
					"id": "tAbovak_anx3Z3KkF",
					"name": "Warp Speed",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Quickens the caster's own nervous system and reflexes to a blur.\n\nDesign: Increased Basic Speed (5 points per +0.25, B) with Warp Sorcery/ Perils, net -30%; the resulting Dodge increase comes free from Basic's normal Speed-to-Dodge derivation, no separate purchase needed. Full modified cost: ~4 points/level; needs Warp Empowerment level 1 (cap 20).",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "mjC-3Y1PWf1e1Ie6k",
							"name": "Warp Sorcery",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "m-m4NjzWMaDNyhZrH",
							"name": "Perils of the Warp",
							"cost_adj": "-10%"
						}
					],
					"points_per_level": 5,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 1
				},
				{
					"id": "tm0uVDKTz6dRqBxHg",
					"name": "Iron Arm",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Hardens flesh and bone into something closer to ceramite for a few seconds.\n\nDesign: Damage Resistance (5/level, B) with Warp Sorcery/Perils, net -30%. Full modified cost: ~4 points/level; needs Warp Empowerment level 1 (cap 20).",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "m_yV6M2O15G8puxFZ",
							"name": "Warp Sorcery",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mz8Zd-olzXVf8VMck",
							"name": "Perils of the Warp",
							"cost_adj": "-10%"
						}
					],
					"points_per_level": 5,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 1
				},
				{
					"id": "tCgzc2qW00vhZpl3T",
					"name": "Haemorrhage",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Ruptures blood vessels inside a target from a distance, with no visible attack to dodge.\n\nDesign: Affliction (10/level, B35) delivering a -20 point bleeding/nauseated disadvantage (+20%), Malediction (+100%, B36, resisted by HT instead of dodged), plus Warp Sorcery/Perils, net +90%. Full modified cost: 10 x 1.9 = 19 points/level; needs Warp Empowerment level 1 (cap 20).",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "mCNIwa83UY8Az7Ke7",
							"name": "Disadvantage Delivered (Bleeding/Nauseated",
							"cost_adj": "+20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mL1I1SX3gCFZJUT6k",
							"name": "Malediction 1",
							"cost_adj": "+100%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mcGi3wUmqbPX1xdc0",
							"name": "Warp Sorcery",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mZArMTFlLvT6o8ITL",
							"name": "Perils of the Warp",
							"cost_adj": "-10%"
						}
					],
					"points_per_level": 10,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 1
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "TAKHtSp5HYhM6fLU2",
			"name": "Divination",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Sight beyond the present moment: warnings, glimpses of the future, remote viewing, and turning fortune against an enemy. Calibrated against Dark Heresy's Divination list (Foreboding, Machinate, Fate's Hand, Scrier's Gaze all map closely) and Black Library's recurring \"the Emperor's seers dream of what is to come\" beats.\n\nDesign: Talent-linked group; see each child.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Psyker",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "t-6wrR80ZLwvorBbs",
					"name": "Foresight",
					"local_notes": "Lore: A flash of true precognition — a moment's warning of what is about to happen.\n\nDesign: Precognition, Basic's core advantage, flat 25, with Warp Sorcery/ Perils, net -30%. Full modified cost: 25 x 0.7 = ~18 points; needs Warp Empowerment level 1 (cap 20). Notably cheap for how strong the fiction makes true precognition sound — a case where a flat Basic advantage's cost doesn't scale with narrative weight the way the leveled Innate Attack-style powers do.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "m-tTd1suudGTqCi0G",
							"name": "Warp Sorcery",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mcrzSDuZ5e10GCmEp",
							"name": "Perils of the Warp",
							"cost_adj": "-10%"
						}
					],
					"base_points": 25
				},
				{
					"id": "tcGzs6xYtyCdaEne6",
					"name": "Forewarning",
					"local_notes": "Lore: An unbidden sense that danger is close, before it strikes.\n\nDesign: Danger Sense, Basic's core advantage, flat 15, with Warp Sorcery/ Perils, net -30%. Full modified cost: 15 x 0.7 = ~11 points; needs Warp Empowerment level 1 (cap 20).",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "mvirmdY7RfY7_nRlh",
							"name": "Warp Sorcery",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mHURgdwPrbdKE33AE",
							"name": "Perils of the Warp",
							"cost_adj": "-10%"
						}
					],
					"base_points": 15
				},
				{
					"id": "tB-YFF1YLY9gNNV8Z",
					"name": "Misfortune",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Turns an enemy's own luck against them — the misfire, the missed step, the wrong turn.\n\nDesign: Affliction (10/level) delivering Unluckiness (-10 points, +10%, matching Basic's own Unluckiness cost), Malediction (+100%), Warp Sorcery/Perils, net +80%. Full modified cost: 10 x 1.8 = 18 points/level; needs Warp Empowerment level 1 (cap 20).",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "mVzlai3Hn2PmQz9gh",
							"name": "Disadvantage Delivered (Unluckiness",
							"cost_adj": "+10%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mLqE5n73coCLl_oDg",
							"name": "Malediction 1",
							"cost_adj": "+100%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mtQ0l-50OZZ6mwAwl",
							"name": "Warp Sorcery",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mN-XHZhYEG7fJGQO-",
							"name": "Perils of the Warp",
							"cost_adj": "-10%"
						}
					],
					"points_per_level": 10,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 1
				},
				{
					"id": "tIpbm5ni7LbhHI0vP",
					"name": "Scrier's Gaze",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Projects the caster's sight to a distant or hidden place.\n\nDesign: Clairsentience, Basic's core advantage, flat 50, with Warp Sorcery/ Perils, net -30%. Full modified cost: 50 x 0.7 = 35 points; needs Warp Empowerment level 3 (cap 40) — one of the pricier single-flat Divination powers.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "mo6fnPOM7jg6H7FQv",
							"name": "Warp Sorcery",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mineVhOzedw-GPNU6",
							"name": "Perils of the Warp",
							"cost_adj": "-10%"
						}
					],
					"base_points": 50
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "T6JWQyzYwe3dhel2o",
			"name": "Pyromancy",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Fire called from nothing, or matter itself set alight and melted. Calibrated against Dark Heresy's Pyromancy list (Fire Bolt, Fire Storm, Molten Beam all appear near-verbatim) and the recurring Black Library image of a pyromancer's target simply combusting.\n\nDesign: Talent-linked group; see each child.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Psyker",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tBFTzPsl9IEp5BhWM",
					"name": "Fire Bolt",
					"local_notes": "Lore: A thrown bolt of raw fire, the pyromancer's most basic attack.\n\nDesign: Innate Attack (Burning, 5/die, B61) with Warp Sorcery/Perils, net -30%. Full modified cost: 5 x 0.7 = 3.5 points/level. Bought at 12 levels (12d burn) for 42 points, the default a trained battlefield psyker buys (a lesser psyker may buy fewer); compare a lasgun's 7d(2) burn. Needs Warp Empowerment level 4 (cap 50) at 12 levels.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "m5x6NwawWO8reS0Da",
							"name": "Warp Sorcery",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "maoOS_PjwULLoZ0ww",
							"name": "Perils of the Warp",
							"cost_adj": "-10%"
						}
					],
					"points_per_level": 5,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 12
				},
				{
					"id": "Tz2Iv1LsMLUKjBmhG",
					"name": "Inferno/Molten Beam",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Two faces of the same power over fire and molten matter: a bursting fireball for a crowd, or a focused, armour-melting beam for a single hard target. A pyromancer trains both together and switches between them freely, never both at once.\n\nDesign: Built as GCS's alternative_abilities container: full price for the costlier child (Molten Beam) plus a fifth the cost of the cheaper one (Inferno), per Basic's Alternate Abilities rule.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"container_type": "alternative_abilities",
					"children": [
						{
							"id": "t_LY9Jpm6R1-5qXgw",
							"name": "Inferno",
							"local_notes": "Lore: A bursting fireball that engulfs a small area.\n\nDesign: Innate Attack (Burning, 5/die) with Explosion level 2 (+100%, B106) plus Warp Sorcery/Perils, net +70%. Full modified cost: 5 x 1.7 = 8.5 points/level. Bought at 8 levels (8d burn ex) for 68 points at full price (charged at a fifth, about 14, as the cheaper alternative ability); a lesser psyker may buy fewer levels. Needs Warp Empowerment level 6 (cap 70) at its full-price rate.",
							"tags": [
								"Advantage",
								"Mental",
								"Psyker",
								"Imperium"
							],
							"modifiers": [
								{
									"id": "my87fKUqJsXEm235s",
									"name": "Explosion",
									"cost_adj": "+100%"
								},
								{
									"id": "mMNWiGc0HaGXRh0WC",
									"name": "Warp Sorcery",
									"cost_adj": "-20%"
								},
								{
									"id": "mNIcO8AbW_xSZfvwb",
									"name": "Perils of the Warp",
									"cost_adj": "-10%"
								}
							],
							"points_per_level": 5,
							"can_level": true,
							"levels": 8
						},
						{
							"id": "tKDUo05aA2x1ooI2L",
							"name": "Molten Beam",
							"local_notes": "Lore: A focused beam of molten matter that burns straight through armour, in the class of a meltagun (8dx6(10) burn) or a lascannon.\n\nDesign: Innate Attack (Burning, 5/die) with Armor Divisor (10) (+200%, B103) plus Warp Sorcery/Perils, net +170%. Full modified cost: 5 x 2.7 = 13.5 points/level. Bought at 12 levels (12d(10) burn) for 162 points, the default a trained battlefield psyker buys (a lesser psyker may buy fewer levels). It is the costlier child, so it sets the alternative_abilities container's cap requirement: Warp Empowerment level 16 (cap 170).",
							"tags": [
								"Advantage",
								"Mental",
								"Psyker",
								"Imperium"
							],
							"modifiers": [
								{
									"id": "mvfKpkx0i4pC5kn0o",
									"name": "Armor Divisor (10)",
									"cost_adj": "+200%"
								},
								{
									"id": "mPLAUZCQK_w-FVDt5",
									"name": "Warp Sorcery",
									"cost_adj": "-20%"
								},
								{
									"id": "mqIWqkSIPx-EiXIpL",
									"name": "Perils of the Warp",
									"cost_adj": "-10%"
								}
							],
							"points_per_level": 5,
							"can_level": true,
							"levels": 12
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "t7IJ9x9Te937ZJq8a",
					"name": "Flame Breath",
					"local_notes": "Lore: A gout of fire breathed out in a cone in front of the caster.\n\nDesign: Innate Attack (Burning, 5/die) with Cone (+50%, B103) plus Warp Sorcery/Perils, net +20%. Full modified cost: 5 x 1.2 = 6 points/level. Bought at 5 levels (5d burn cone) for 30 points, a heavy flamer's damage; a lesser psyker may buy fewer levels. Needs Warp Empowerment level 2 (cap 30) at 5 levels.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "md0hj2FfJ2bx2a1tY",
							"name": "Cone",
							"cost_adj": "+50%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mq_5lZ-FUUKm7SXy3",
							"name": "Warp Sorcery",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mjcXmUUvzGtlOBzqi",
							"name": "Perils of the Warp",
							"cost_adj": "-10%"
						}
					],
					"points_per_level": 5,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 5
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "TdtXAi4pelDbr5lIP",
			"name": "Telekinesis",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Force of will made physical: hurled objects, barriers of solid air, crushing grips, and — at its rarest and most dangerous — stepping instantly from one place to another. Calibrated against Dark Heresy's Telekinesis list (Assail, Kinetic Barrier/Shield, Crush, Warp Conduit/Gate of Infinity all map closely).\n\nDesign: Talent-linked group; see each child.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Psyker",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tpTAv3vc7HVMcvUM4",
					"name": "Assail",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Hurls the nearest loose object, or the target themselves, with bruising force.\n\nDesign: Innate Attack (Crushing, 5/die, B61) with Warp Sorcery/Perils, net -30%. Full modified cost: 5 x 0.7 = 3.5 points/level. Bought at 8 levels (8d cr) for 28 points, the default a trained battlefield psyker buys (a lesser psyker may buy fewer). Needs Warp Empowerment level 2 (cap 30) at 8 levels.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "mnTUz43M59NkVNpFa",
							"name": "Warp Sorcery",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mlKRPhUsarsbJOKJp",
							"name": "Perils of the Warp",
							"cost_adj": "-10%"
						}
					],
					"points_per_level": 5,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 8
				},
				{
					"id": "Th73HnX3BhT9_T31Y",
					"name": "Force Dome/Kinetic Shield",
					"local_notes": "Lore: The same telekinetic barrier, bought as one power: held tight around the caster alone, or opened out to cover the whole squad.\n\nDesign: Alternative_abilities container; full price for the costlier Force Dome plus a fifth of Kinetic Shield.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"container_type": "alternative_abilities",
					"children": [
						{
							"id": "tWUwJc1ZgFP34zuy1",
							"name": "Kinetic Shield",
							"local_notes": "Lore: A tight telekinetic skin around the caster alone.\n\nDesign: Damage Resistance (5/level, B), self only, with Warp Sorcery/ Perils, net -30%. Full modified cost: 5 x 0.7 = ~4 points/level (discounted to a fifth as the cheaper alternative ability); needs Warp Empowerment level 1 (cap 20) at its full-price rate.",
							"tags": [
								"Advantage",
								"Mental",
								"Psyker",
								"Imperium"
							],
							"modifiers": [
								{
									"id": "mlVT956nSPLkYuhlJ",
									"name": "Warp Sorcery",
									"cost_adj": "-20%"
								},
								{
									"id": "mwITTz-j2P1vEYr36",
									"name": "Perils of the Warp",
									"cost_adj": "-10%"
								}
							],
							"points_per_level": 5,
							"can_level": true,
							"levels": 1
						},
						{
							"id": "tpN0Ool5nEBPhbcK2",
							"name": "Force Dome",
							"local_notes": "Lore: A dome of solid force wide enough to cover the caster's whole fireteam.\n\nDesign: Damage Resistance (5/level) with Area Effect (+50%, B102, 2-yard radius) plus Warp Sorcery/Perils, net +20%. Full modified cost: 5 x 1.2 = 6 points/level (the costlier child, so it sets the container's cap requirement); needs Warp Empowerment level 1 (cap 20).",
							"tags": [
								"Advantage",
								"Mental",
								"Psyker",
								"Imperium"
							],
							"modifiers": [
								{
									"id": "mQVQmX469wb8ygk9I",
									"name": "Area Effect",
									"cost_adj": "+50%"
								},
								{
									"id": "mYrlm7Q-dOS0ZXlhq",
									"name": "Warp Sorcery",
									"cost_adj": "-20%"
								},
								{
									"id": "m3v1DK7ilkwkXMZc9",
									"name": "Perils of the Warp",
									"cost_adj": "-10%"
								}
							],
							"points_per_level": 5,
							"can_level": true,
							"levels": 1
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "tXGNRQ0bJSnvFH5jW",
					"name": "Crush",
					"local_notes": "Lore: An invisible telekinetic grip that closes on a target's throat or chest, ignoring armour and impossible to dodge.\n\nDesign: Innate Attack (Crushing, 5/die) with Malediction (+100%, B36) and Armor Divisor (2) (+50%, B103), plus Warp Sorcery/Perils, net +120%. Full modified cost: 5 x 2.2 = 11 points/level. Bought at 8 levels (8d(2) cr, Malediction) for 88 points, the default a trained battlefield psyker buys (a lesser psyker may buy fewer). Needs Warp Empowerment level 8 (cap 90) at 8 levels.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "mx1QyYeOwMZaDXU_G",
							"name": "Malediction 1",
							"cost_adj": "+100%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mAZyYkEyHHHfYLJIN",
							"name": "Armor Divisor (2)",
							"cost_adj": "+50%"
						},
						{
							"id": "m46Cfk6RKYMxG2UEU",
							"name": "Warp Sorcery",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mLG5Y1x9FLHdY4Pai",
							"name": "Perils of the Warp",
							"cost_adj": "-10%"
						}
					],
					"points_per_level": 5,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 8
				},
				{
					"id": "tEgdysAWIOP3t2fe0",
					"name": "Gate of Infinity",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Tears a hole between two points in real space and steps through — the rarest and most feared telekinetic feat, since a botched Gate can open into the warp itself instead.\n\nDesign: Built on Basic's own Warp advantage (B99, instant travel to any place you have seen/visualized, flat 100), with Preparation Required (-20%, B113, a few seconds' concentration) and the Severe Perils tier, reflecting the setting's specific fear of a failed Gate opening into the immaterium. Net -60%. Full modified cost: 100 x 0.4 = 40 points — the single most expensive non-Great-Power ability in this file; needs Warp Empowerment level 3 (cap 40), the minimum at which \"Delta and up\" can cast the full non-Great-Power roster, exactly on the cap with no headroom to spare.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "md6jyfQF3hboLjZmt",
							"name": "Preparation Required",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mXf3b2GJx5O2g5ER9",
							"name": "Warp Sorcery",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mYSnkSW2x2eZsHjdl",
							"name": "Perils of the Warp (Severe)",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						}
					],
					"base_points": 100
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "T8kCjTOyeAKu7GQSw",
			"name": "Telepathy",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Reading, sending, and overwhelming minds. Calibrated against Dark Heresy's Telepathy list (Mind Probe, Dominate, Psychic Scream, Terrify, Invisibility-adjacent Mental Interrogation) and the astropathic relay seen throughout Black Library whenever a ship needs to send word home.\n\nDesign: Talent-linked group; see each child.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Psyker",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "Tdomw2vBoXhmijqkk",
					"name": "Mind Probe/Dominate",
					"local_notes": "Lore: The same intrusion into another mind, bought at two intensities: a forced reading of buried memory, or outright control of the body.\n\nDesign: Alternative_abilities container; full price for the costlier Dominate plus a fifth of Mind Probe.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"container_type": "alternative_abilities",
					"children": [
						{
							"id": "tSuAfr3NbeG3VsCWN",
							"name": "Mind Probe",
							"local_notes": "Lore: Tears buried memories and secrets from an unwilling subject.\n\nDesign: Mind Probe, Basic's core advantage, flat 20, with Warp Sorcery/ Perils, net -30%. Full modified cost: 20 x 0.7 = 14 points (discounted to a fifth as the cheaper alternative ability); needs Warp Empowerment level 1 (cap 20) at its full-price rate.",
							"tags": [
								"Advantage",
								"Mental",
								"Psyker",
								"Imperium"
							],
							"modifiers": [
								{
									"id": "mFMvLYSXYVI76jL8R",
									"name": "Warp Sorcery",
									"cost_adj": "-20%"
								},
								{
									"id": "mudovOg9iCOHR-Pm1",
									"name": "Perils of the Warp",
									"cost_adj": "-10%"
								}
							],
							"base_points": 20
						},
						{
							"id": "tnpOVCfggNf7M-ALB",
							"name": "Dominate",
							"local_notes": "Lore: Seizes outright control of a target's body and actions.\n\nDesign: Mind Control, Basic's core advantage, flat 50, with Warp Sorcery/Perils, net -30%. Full modified cost: 50 x 0.7 = 35 points (the costlier child, so it sets the container's cap requirement); needs Warp Empowerment level 3 (cap 40).",
							"tags": [
								"Advantage",
								"Mental",
								"Psyker",
								"Imperium"
							],
							"modifiers": [
								{
									"id": "mtyVXGWIZFR7ryD68",
									"name": "Warp Sorcery",
									"cost_adj": "-20%"
								},
								{
									"id": "mQiucht6C5gsfP80t",
									"name": "Perils of the Warp",
									"cost_adj": "-10%"
								}
							],
							"base_points": 50
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "t2Xnur8uK3mA4BRbP",
					"name": "Psychic Scream",
					"local_notes": "Lore: A silent, mind-shattering shout that stuns everyone nearby.\n\nDesign: Affliction (10/level, delivering the default Stun effect) with Area Effect (+50%) plus Warp Sorcery/Perils, net +20%. Full modified cost: 10 x 1.2 = 12 points/level; needs Warp Empowerment level 1 (cap 20).",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "mkErZORa9B48Us9X2",
